WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.440
There businesses all over the country

00:00:01.880 --> 00:00:05.760
right now who are sitting on companies

00:00:03.440 --> 00:00:07.360
worth six and seven figures and they

00:00:05.760 --> 00:00:09.440
would sell it to you for absolutely

00:00:07.360 --> 00:00:11.400
nothing. Not because the business is bad

00:00:09.440 --> 00:00:13.440
but because the owner is done. They're

00:00:11.400 --> 00:00:15.600
tired, they're ready to retire and most

00:00:13.440 --> 00:00:17.480
of them do not have a kid or a partner

00:00:15.600 --> 00:00:19.480
lined up to take it over. So they're

00:00:17.480 --> 00:00:21.440
stuck with one real option and that is

00:00:19.480 --> 00:00:22.840
to ultimately sell the business. And

00:00:21.440 --> 00:00:25.200
when that is the only option what they

00:00:22.840 --> 00:00:27.200
want the most isn't a big check on day

00:00:25.200 --> 00:00:28.880
one. It's to get made whole over the

00:00:27.200 --> 00:00:30.920
course of time from somebody who's

00:00:28.880 --> 00:00:32.320
actually going to keep the business

00:00:30.920 --> 00:00:34.680
running and take care of the customers

00:00:32.320 --> 00:00:36.040
that they spent decades building trust

00:00:34.680 --> 00:00:37.960
with. So today I'm going to be walking

00:00:36.040 --> 00:00:40.120
you through the five businesses that you

00:00:37.960 --> 00:00:41.520
can buy without writing any check at all

00:00:40.120 --> 00:00:43.120
and at the end of each one I'm going to

00:00:41.520 --> 00:00:45.000
give you real ways that people can

00:00:43.120 --> 00:00:47.000
structure these types of deals. You

00:00:45.000 --> 00:00:48.600
don't need an inheritance or rich uncle

00:00:47.000 --> 00:00:50.400
to make any of this work. You just need

00:00:48.600 --> 00:00:51.880
to find the right business and structure

00:00:50.400 --> 00:00:53.400
it the right way. And before we jump

00:00:51.880 --> 00:00:54.720
into any of this, my name is Austin

00:00:53.400 --> 00:00:56.720
Zaback and I've built multiple

00:00:54.720 --> 00:00:58.280
businesses across real estate and pest

00:00:56.720 --> 00:01:00.360
control and a handful of other

00:00:58.280 --> 00:01:01.680
industries over the last 10 years. So

00:01:00.360 --> 00:01:03.200
here's the thing that nobody's talking

00:01:01.680 --> 00:01:05.400
about enough. We're in the middle of the

00:01:03.200 --> 00:01:08.120
largest transfer in business ownership

00:01:05.400 --> 00:01:10.600
in American history. Roughly 10,000 baby

00:01:08.120 --> 00:01:12.480
boomers are retiring every single day in

00:01:10.600 --> 00:01:15.040
this country and a huge chunk of them

00:01:12.480 --> 00:01:17.240
own small businesses especially in home

00:01:15.040 --> 00:01:18.920
service and in the trades. And these are

00:01:17.240 --> 00:01:21.680
companies that have been running for 20,

00:01:18.920 --> 00:01:23.640
30 or even 40 years. Industry estimates

00:01:21.680 --> 00:01:25.960
project that trillions of dollars in

00:01:23.640 --> 00:01:28.480
business value is going to change hands

00:01:25.960 --> 00:01:30.480
over the next decade as this generation

00:01:28.480 --> 00:01:32.200
exits. And that is exactly where you

00:01:30.480 --> 00:01:34.400
come in because when an owner doesn't

00:01:32.200 --> 00:01:36.320
have a clean exit lined up, they get

00:01:34.400 --> 00:01:37.680
really flexible. So let's start with one

00:01:36.320 --> 00:01:39.200
that doesn't get talked about enough and

00:01:37.680 --> 00:01:41.160
that is electrical. Because while

00:01:39.200 --> 00:01:43.200
everybody's chasing software companies

00:01:41.160 --> 00:01:45.160
and online businesses, America is

00:01:43.200 --> 00:01:46.560
quietly running out of electricians.

00:01:45.160 --> 00:01:48.960
Studies are actually projecting a

00:01:46.560 --> 00:01:51.520
shortfall of 250,000

00:01:48.960 --> 00:01:53.320
electricians by 2030. And that is a huge

00:01:51.520 --> 00:01:55.320
problem and it's only getting worse.

00:01:53.320 --> 00:01:57.000
It's essential, it's licensed and the

00:01:55.320 --> 00:01:58.840
barrier to entry for a brand new

00:01:57.000 --> 00:02:00.600
competitor is really high because you

00:01:58.840 --> 00:02:02.640
need real expertise and real

00:02:00.600 --> 00:02:04.880
certifications to be able to operate.

00:02:02.640 --> 00:02:07.120
And that protects existing businesses

00:02:04.880 --> 00:02:09.399
from getting steamrolled by some random

00:02:07.120 --> 00:02:11.480
new startup undercutting prices. And the

00:02:09.399 --> 00:02:13.440
data actually backs this up. So, the US

00:02:11.480 --> 00:02:15.640
electrical industry is projected to hit

00:02:13.440 --> 00:02:18.080
over 347

00:02:15.640 --> 00:02:20.120
billion in revenue in 2026. And

00:02:18.080 --> 00:02:23.080
top-performing electrical contractors

00:02:20.120 --> 00:02:25.120
are running net margins north of 20%.

00:02:23.080 --> 00:02:27.320
Electrical businesses tend to have less

00:02:25.120 --> 00:02:28.600
recurring subscription-style revenue

00:02:27.320 --> 00:02:30.000
than some of the others that we're going

00:02:28.600 --> 00:02:31.840
